commit 8f99bc3bea838fac0f23f698d5cf44069c9c12d4
Author: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date:   Wed Jun 17 07:53:59 2026 +0000

    chore: isolate tigrao fsm plugin skeleton
    
    ### Motivation
    
    - Prepare an isolated, non‑connected skeleton of the Tigrão FSM plugin inside the TR4 codebase so future porting can be incremental and safe.
    - Encapsulate the Tigrão FSM private-state and UI primitives (callbacks, button styles, session) without touching the main bot, dispatcher or any musical flows.
    
    ### Description
    
    - Added a new plugin folder `app/plugins/tigrao_fsm/` with core stubs and utilities: `__init__.py`, `README.md`, `mount.py`, `plugin.py`, `state.py`, `storage.py`, `permissions.py`, `keyboards.py`, `texts.py`, plus `routers/` and `runtime/` stub files for future areas.
    - Implemented an in‑memory Tigrão session FSM in `state.py` preserving the original design (session fields, 15 min timeout, ContextVar), explicitly not using `aiogram.fsm`.
    - Introduced a centralized callback namespace `tgf:` and helper functions plus a small button specification utility supporting `primary`, `success` and `danger` styles in `keyboards.py`.
    - Left all runtime hooks and routers as inactive stubs and documented DM-only panel policy and migration notes in `README.md`; no dispatcher registration, no imports of `app.main`, and no changes to musical flows.
    
    ### Testing
    
    - Ran `python -m compileall -q app` which succeeded with no syntax errors.
    - Added and executed static tests in `tests/test_tigrao_fsm_skeleton.py` with `python -m pytest -q tests/test_tigrao_fsm_skeleton.py`, which passed (7 tests).
    - Executed the full test suite with `python -m pytest -q`; the suite ran but produced failures unrelated to the new skeleton (94 failing tests, 616 passed); these failures reflect pre-existing expectations in other modules and not the plugin changes.
    - Produced required review artifacts under `artifacts/codex_reports/` including the step report, full diff and branch status for external review.
